As an AI & Cloud Application Security Specialist, you will influence how cloud applications and AI-enabled solutions are assessed, secured and governed, turning complex security requirements into practical guidance that enables innovation while protecting our global business. 
 You will combine hands-on security assessments with consulting, governance, and cross-functional collaboration:
 Evaluate, review, and approve AI-enabled applications and SaaS solutions.
 Assess SaaS solutions, products, and architecture documentation for security risks, regulatory requirements, and compliance.
 Review AI and SaaS applications and features, provide security consulting, and contribute to the development of internal security guardrails, standards, and guidelines.
 Review security assessments and checklists, document outcomes, and approve solutions within delegated authority.
 Provide cybersecurity consulting to IT and business stakeholders, with a focus on AI, cloud, and SaaS-related initiatives.
 Support cybersecurity audits, testing activities, and security assessments, and help stakeholders remediate identified findings.
 Review, and support the definition and maintenance of cybersecurity rules, standards, guidelines, and checklists for AI and SaaS security, and advise stakeholders on their implementation.
 Drive the secure adoption of emerging AI and cloud technologies by balancing business enablement, innovation, risk management, and regulatory compliance, collaborating with architecture, legal, privacy, procurement, and business teams to ensure it.
Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Cybersecurity, Information Security, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a comparable qualification supported by relevant professional experience.
 At least five years of experience in enterprise IT, including a minimum of three years in cybersecurity, application security, cloud security, or a related field.
 Practical experience assessing applications, cloud services, SaaS solutions, architectures, and AI-enabled solutions for security risks and compliance requirements.
 Experience applying industry standards and frameworks such as OWASP, NIST, CIS Controls, ISO/IEC 27001, or comparable security frameworks.
 Solid understanding of cloud security concepts, web application security, identity and access management, authentication mechanisms, and encryption technologies.
 Knowledge of AI security concepts, AI governance, secure AI adoption, and risks associated with AI-enabled applications is highly desirable.
 Ability to analyze complex technical topics and translate security requirements into practical guidance for technical and non-technical stakeholders.
 Strong communication and consulting skills, with the ability to influence decisions and drive secure outcomes across international and cross-functional teams.
 Professional proficiency in English, min. B2.
 Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CCSP, CSSLP, Azure Security Engineer, AWS Security Specialty, or equivalent certifications are advantageous.
